DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  pptthhrreeaadd__aattffoorrkk()  function  registers fork handlers that are to be
       executed when ffoorrkk(2) is called by any thread in a process.   The  han‐
       dlers are executed in the context of the thread that calls ffoorrkk(2).

       Three kinds of handler can be registered:

       •  _p_r_e_p_a_r_e  specifies  a handler that is executed in the parent process
          before ffoorrkk(2) processing starts.

       •  _p_a_r_e_n_t specifies a handler that is executed in  the  parent  process
          after ffoorrkk(2) processing completes.

       •  _c_h_i_l_d  specifies a handler that is executed in the child process af‐
          ter ffoorrkk(2) processing completes.

       Any of the three arguments may be NULL if no handler is needed  in  the
       corresponding phase of ffoorrkk(2) processing.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, pptthhrreeaadd__aattffoorrkk() returns zero.  On error, it returns an er‐
       ror number.  pptthhrreeaadd__aattffoorrkk() may be called multiple times by a process
       to  register  additional  handlers.   The  handlers  for each phase are
       called in a specified order: the _p_r_e_p_a_r_e handlers are called in reverse
       order of registration; the _p_a_r_e_n_t and _c_h_i_l_d handlers are called in  the
       order of registration.

